# P2 runtime guard research — source-only design

Baseline: PR5995 `4f4159820c37f01d245784d1186bd51fcbc8ebb6`, native-C complete qualification. Canonical planning main is `19fdb086ea96af9a9f87936a2b888e10af4ed810`; no scientific migration is proposed. Local file hashes were checked: `native_backend.py` = `e473c38245c3668715b5a78dfe980b2fe3ed0d0c9b8c97c666fbae6ecf1fffd5`; `finite_controls.py` = `df989a831aac43cc1af95169dad8c64a7548760e6e1f96976da996703f2c8f7a`; `native_gf2.c` = `e9c3c9194a08718bd1575c1cf08c6c6772d3b644c2e274c25a84a1f9249d06cc`. Full pins and references are in PROPOSAL.json.

## Primary design

In `RuntimeGuard.__init__` (159–182), preserve the first occurrence of each function object using `is`, then snapshot each distinct object's code, globals, effective builtins, defaults, keyword defaults, closure and cells exactly as before. A tiny nested identity scan avoids introducing hashing, equality callbacks or a new builtin dependency. Distinct functions sharing code must remain distinct. Source helpers, class slots and native slots retain their separate checks even when they point to already-recorded functions.

In `check` (184–209), replace each `require(condition, message)` with an explicit failing branch and the same anchored RuntimeError/message. Preserve expression order and short-circuit order. Concatenated messages are constructed only when their predicate fails. Attribute-access exceptions continue to propagate; an empty captured cell continues to raise `ValueError("Cell is empty")`, rather than being converted to a drift error.

For traced binding, the source constructs 13 records: four original helpers, four original Label methods, four current methods, and current rank. Original `__init__` and `contains` repeat, giving 11 distinct objects. Untraced binding also repeats rank, giving 10. The successful path constructs 30 name-bearing messages: six globals, fourteen builtins, eight class members, two native entries. Across the stated 298,644 complete kernel calls this removes 597,288 repeated function-record visits, 3,583,728 repeated attribute identity checks and 8,959,320 string concatenation evaluations. These are source-derived counts, not timings; constructor/final and finite-control checks are additional. No speed factor is inferred. `CALL-BUDGET.json` itemizes 61 eliminated successful helper calls per traced check, 59 retained distinct predicates, 36 retained explicit lookup/type/length calls and every new cost.

## Ownership and integration

Implement only `guard_candidate.py`, `guard_controls.py` and lane documentation inside this owned directory after approval. Export a factory `make_runtime_guard(backend)` returning a compatible class with the original constructor and `check` signatures and fields. Parent installs it only into the isolated candidate backend before binding. The factory does not alter source modules, arithmetic, observers, counters, baseline classes or shared harnesses.

Parent must finalize all helper/trace replacements and runtime closure-cell values before invoking the constructor. Retain constructor `self.check()`, both wrapper-entry checks (339 and 361), and `full_driver.py:291` final check. Each entry still checks before tracing, eligibility, native execution or fallback. Integration cannot reuse a captured guard after changing wrappers. No cached PASS or once-per-run replacement is allowed.

## Retained contract and bill

Keep cold source authentication, builtin/integer-descriptor admission, source class shape, original arithmetic and dense independent oracle, all finite cases, every live distinct freshness predicate, failures and final observations. The supported contract remains serial execution with no mutation during a call; arbitrary backend/process-memory mutation and concurrent/reentrant mutation are outside it. Identity checks retain their existing granularity: this is no new deep-content detector.

New costs are candidate source copy/authentication/import, class-factory creation, cold deduplication, retained strong-reference records, additional differential finite controls and serialized receipts. Existing native cold compile/load remains; no new compiler unit is required. All costs enter the complete candidate bill. Baseline controls execute unchanged against its original guard; candidate controls execute against the installed class, with separate backend/source instances.

## Controls and discriminating next test

Retain every existing finite/normal/O control. Add first-occurrence record-order and exact-identity inventory checks for traced/untraced binds; retain distinct functions with equal code. Differentially mutate code/defaults/kwdefaults of every distinct saved function, wrapper/traced-rank cells (including deletion), all relevant global/builtin/class/native slots, and simultaneous drifts to check first-failure precedence. Restore mutations in finally. Compare exact outcome type/message and unchanged native/fallback counters, observer receipts and helper callback logs; exercise both wrapper entries on native-eligible and unsupported-width/container inputs. Shared runtime-cell mutation must compare actual baseline exceptions as well as direct held-guard checks. Test PASS, later mutation, then rejection to exclude stale acceptance.

After source review, parent runs this finite matrix against untouched PR5995 and candidate, then one complete cold B/C pilot with all control costs. Exact output/call/trace equality is mandatory; complete wall/CPU determine disposition. The combined 15% goal is not an individual promise.

## Source-only alternatives and C hazards

A C loop could reduce interpreter dispatch but adds compilation, state ownership, cleanup and error-conversion work. Public [function APIs](https://docs.python.org/3.12/c-api/function.html) expose borrowed code/globals/defaults/closure references; optional NULL values need Python-None normalization. The [3.12.3 header](https://github.com/python/cpython/blob/v3.12.3/Include/cpython/funcobject.h) excludes function APIs from the limited API and supplies no builtins getter; use checked attribute access rather than private layout assumptions. [Dictionary APIs](https://docs.python.org/3.12/c-api/dict.html) require error-aware lookup, and [cell APIs](https://docs.python.org/3.12/c-api/cell.html) alone do not reproduce Python empty-cell exceptions; [cell source](https://github.com/python/cpython/blob/v3.12.3/Objects/cellobject.c) establishes that behavior. Strong references, GIL-held serial checks and every error cleanup path need review. No broad portability claim is warranted. Watcher/version-based PASS caches are rejected: they omit required live reads and closure-cell coverage. First test the smaller Python change; a native alternative requires a new gate.
